{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"d18a80ba5ca953eed687fc40454a7fe2b93ea739336d9f949027c94a3d28a243","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_0cf13f8ac6a5026ef4a9ab7f5daec0ec1eb3c719b06b3386c6c639fee24947b2","overall_assessment":"The paper is generally well-organized, with a logical flow from theoretical preliminaries to empirical validation. The mathematical notation is consistent and clearly defined, and the algorithms are presented with sufficient detail for reproduction. The main clarity weakness lies in the presentation of the structured sparse approximation operator, where the definition of the upsampling switch variable is ambiguous, and the visual aids rely on captions that do not fully specify the experimental parameters used in the plots.","paper_id":"B1mAJI9gl","paper_identity_sha256":"dac5ed8cb5ec59a142a071572f6e3a81dbda95f8f306a23b4ed5cdf2c67e9b9a","prompt_identity_sha256":"e8f502cceccb090141372b658b60b5a550db85e190bd6031c33e30c56699b8eb","raw_response_sha256":"a5a318b03dbe297937a5a8a5b903e552f0e3871d02ac9f39eaf8f54b15b2de86","request_identity_sha256":"d21e19d1e3e5acd594abb5cad8dfb51b7f4e42a60047de5dc8d87a7eabc1c9b7","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"ae94a46385b13489f484c6ce7dc8190db552b3ac4dad866f72426b7dc5e17d5d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-017"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured, moving logically from the introduction of the invertibility problem to the theoretical model and finally to empirical validation. The terminology is precise, with key concepts like 'model-RIP' and 'model-k-sparse' clearly defined in the preliminaries. However, the presentation of the structured sparse approximation algorithm M(z, k) in Section 2.3 has a minor clarity issue. The text defines M(z, k) using an upsampling operator with a switch variable s, but the specific definition of s is not explicitly provided in the immediate context, only referenced as 'upsampling switches'. While the special cases M_known and M_fixed are defined, the general case's dependency on s could be more explicitly linked to the pooling operation to avoid ambiguity for readers implementing the general algorithm.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. The paper clearly defines the dimensions of the input signal x, the filter matrix W, and the hidden activations h. The definitions of the Restricted Isometry Property (RIP) and the model-RIP condition are standard and clearly stated. The notation for the sparsity model M_k and its linear combination M_k^2 is introduced logically. The equations for the reconstruction error bounds are presented with clear variable definitions. There are no significant inconsistencies in the use of symbols throughout the theoretical sections.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-009","SRC-031","SRC-033","SRC-037"],"review_text":"The figure captions provide detailed descriptions of the visual content. For instance, the caption for Figure 1 clearly defines the matrix W and the filter bank structure. The captions for Figures 2 and 3 describe the histograms of empirical model-RIP values and the reconstruction errors, specifying the parameters used (e.g., filter sizes, sparsity levels). However, the caption for Figure 3 (referenced in SRC-037) describes the recovery of z by Algorithm 2 but does not explicitly state the value of the regularization parameter lambda used in the algorithm, which is a key hyperparameter for the reconstruction. Providing this value in the caption or the main text would improve the reproducibility of the results shown in the figure.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"152caf2d2287f20093313f7139326846ae6794b2fef7f58db651a8846c7e2e6e","paper_id":"B1mAJI9gl","paper_ordinal":14,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"a5a318b03dbe297937a5a8a5b903e552f0e3871d02ac9f39eaf8f54b15b2de86","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1mAJI9gl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"b45d8bbf120138bdccf751ed1fdaabefc3ea08955aa0b73d7ba42623e3a833e0","request_identity_sha256":"d21e19d1e3e5acd594abb5cad8dfb51b7f4e42a60047de5dc8d87a7eabc1c9b7","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":758,"prompt_tokens":19223,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19981},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"d21e19d1e3e5acd594abb5cad8dfb51b7f4e42a60047de5dc8d87a7eabc1c9b7","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}